  "solution": {
    "text": "The quantity $h v / K_{\\mathrm{B}}$ corresponds to temperature. $h v=3 / 2 K_{\\mathrm{B}} T$\r\nwhere, $T=$ temperature $K_{\\mathrm{B}}=$ Boltzmann constant $$\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\n\\frac{h v}{K_{B}}=\\frac{3}{2} T\r\n\\end{array}\r\n$$\r\nsince, $\\frac{3}{2}$ is a constant, the value of $\\frac{h v}{K_{\\mathrm{B}}}$ corresponds\r\nto temperature. Therefore option\r\n(c) is correct.",
    "image": null
  },
